WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.375
The review opens right in Claude Code, beside the chat.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.125
Comment on any line, and blueprint takes it into the next revision.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.325
Reviews live where the team already reads docs.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.055
Every review opens with a picture of the change.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.100
The change splits into pull requests, stacked or side by side.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.825
Approve the plan, and start each group from the pane.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.549
Blueprint can also draw the repo as a map: every capability, the code it owns, and what it requires.

00:00:49.355 --> 00:00:52.605
Capabilities that share files are tied together.

00:00:56.758 --> 00:01:01.583
When a pull request moves the code under a spec, CI says which spec to check.

00:01:02.188 --> 00:01:05.663
And which docs outside the repo may need an update.

00:01:06.468 --> 00:01:09.943
Specs and code stay honest, in both directions.
